      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the test cases removed from `core/fxge/android/cfpf_skiafontmgr_unittest.cpp` have been equivalently ported to `core/fxge/android/cfx_androidfontinfo_unittest.cpp`, with the exception of two tests that were specifically verifying an old bug/quirk that this refactor fixes. Here is the exact mapping of the removed test cases to the added ones:1. **`CreateFontPreferOriginalNonCJK`** ➡️ **`MapFontPreferOriginalNonCJK`**   *(Verifies that exact name matches are preferred over substitutions for non-CJK fonts)*2. **`CreateFontFallbackToSubstNonCJK`** ➡️ **`MapFontFallbackToSubstNonCJK`**   *(Verifies that missing non-CJK fonts correctly fall back to their substitutions)*3. **`CreateFontPreferOriginalCJK`** ➡️ **`MapFontPreferOriginalCJK`**   *(Verifies that exact name matches are preferred for CJK fonts, even if another CJK font has a higher glyph count)*4. **`CreateFontFallbackToSubstCJK`** ➡️ **`MapFontFallbackToSubstCJK`**   *(Verifies that missing CJK fonts correctly fall back to their substitutions)*5. **`CreateFontCJKFallbackNoMatch`** ➡️ **`MapFontCJKFallbackNoMatch`**   *(Verifies that an unknown CJK font falls back to the available CJK font)*6. **`CreateFontCJKDifferentGlyphCountsNoNameMatch`** ➡️ **`MapFontCJKDifferentGlyphCountsNoNameMatch`**   *(Verifies that when falling back between multiple CJK fonts without a name match, the one with the higher glyph count is chosen)*### What about the `CreateFontCJKOrderDependency` tests?The removed test file had two order dependency tests:* `CreateFontCJKOrderDependency1`* `CreateFontCJKOrderDependency2`These tests were removed because they verified an artifact of the old single-pass matching logic. In the old `CFPF_SkiaFontMgr`, searching for a CJK font would sometimes pick a font with a higher glyph count instead of a perfect name match just because of the order the system scanned the font files. By rewriting `CFX_AndroidFontInfo` to inherit from `CFX_FolderFontInfo`, the search is now properly done in two passes:1. Try to find a perfect name match (`FindFont(..., must_match_name\u003dtrue)`).2. If that fails, fall back to comparing glyph counts (`FindFont(..., must_match_name\u003dfalse)`).This eliminates the order dependency quirk altogether, making those two tests obsolete (the correct behavior is now robustly covered by `MapFontPreferOriginalCJK`).### New CoverageThe CL also adds **`MapFontCJKDifferentWeights`**, which wasn\u0027t in the old test file. This improves coverage by verifying that style/weight matching now works correctly for CJK fonts, a feature inherited from the new `CFX_FolderFontInfo` base class.",
